          "reply": "Infinity’s discounts are broader than one isolated sunscreen offer, but I can’t confirm a named, time-limited campaign. The clearest pattern is several SPF products presented as 1+1 promo packs, alongside separate discounts on regular listings.\n\n- **Sunscreens:** the official pages show 1+1 packs for Ultra Fluid, lotion, Hydro Boost gel, kids’ lotion, mist, tinted, and Velvet Touch. Separate cream listings show 40% off; for example, the all-skin-types SPF 50+ cream is listed at EGP 340, reduced to EGP 204. The “only 10 items left” message appears on several pages, but doesn’t prove stock is actually low or that they’re clearing it. [Ultra Fluid](https://infinityclinicpharma.com/products/infinity-care-sunscreen-ultra-fluid-spf50-1-1) · [Hydro Boost gel](https://infinityclinicpharma.com/products/infinity-care-hydro-boost-gel-spf50-promopack) · [Sunscreen cream](https://infinityclinicpharma.com/products/infinity-naturals-sunscreen-cream-spf-50-all-skin-types)\n- **Moisturizers:** I found regular cream listings displaying 40% discounts, plus a separate day-and-night cream duo advertised as 1+1. Infinity’s daily acne moisturizer page confirms its positioning, but didn’t show a price or offer when I read it. [Moisturizing cream](https://infinityclinicpharma.com/products/infinity-moisturizing-cream) · [Day + night duo](https://infinityclinicpharma.com/products/infinity-collagen-anti-aging-day-night-50ml-1-1) · [Acne daily moisturizer](https://infinityclinicpharma.com/products/infinity-daily-moisturizing-cream)\n\n**What history adds:** the watched Infinity pages have price/stock readings from Oct 1–10, but no recorded changes. That’s a limited set of products, and these snapshots don’t capture offer terms or when they began—so it doesn’t establish how long the deals have run. [Infinity’s terms](https://infinityclinicpharma.com/pages/terms-conditions) refer to “Big Deals and offers” and limit customers to one order during them. That supports the possibility of a broader deals period, but doesn’t confirm these listings belong to one current campaign.\n\n**Possible explanation:** several 1+1 packs across different sunscreen types look like a deliberate multi-product promotion, and the one-order rule may be intended to limit repeat ordering during deals. But Infinity doesn’t state why these offers are running. I found no proof of clearance, a seasonal reason, or a response to competitors.\n\nChecked Oct 10, 2026, Cairo time.",
